llowed when theu800 area isu800 inactive iu800u82eeu800. theu800 hazardous activity isu800 notu800 taking place oru800 when au800 specific clearance hasu800 been obtained. inu800 theu800 usu800 restricted areas carry theu800 prefix \"ru800\". pilots approaching au800 restricted area should contact theu800 controlling authority oru800 atcu800 tou800 confirm current activity status. military operations areas moau800 military operations areas moau800 military operations areas moau800 au800 military operations area isu800 au800 block ofu800 airspace established tou800  separate certain military training activities from ifru800 traffic  andu800 tou800 identify foru800 vfru800 traffic where those activities take place. moas areu800 nonregulatory u8e28094 they dou800 notu800 legally prohibit civilian entry u8e28094 butu800 they areu800 au800 significant hazard indicator. activities conducted within active moas include airu800 combat manoeuvres intercepts aerobatics formation training andu800 lowu800 altitude tactics. military aircraft inu800 anu800 active moau800 mayu800 operate atu800 high speeds andu800 inu800 ways that areu800 unpredictable tou800 civilian traffic. when au800 moau800 isu800 active ifru800 traffic will beu800 rerouted oru800 held clear byu800 atcu800 unless separation canu800 beu800 positively assured. vfru800 pilots mayu800 legally enter anu800 active moau800 without au800 clearance butu800 this isu800 strongly inadvisable without first confirming activity status with atcu800 oru800 flight service. onu800 sectional charts moas areu800 shown with magenta hashed boundaries andu800 areu800 labelled with their name vertical limits andu800 controlling agency frequency. warning areas warning areas warning areas warning areas areu800 similar inu800 character tou800 moas butu800 areu800 located inu800  international airspace  beyond 12u800 nmu800 from theu800 usu800 coastline where theu800 faau800 does notu800 have theu800 same authority tou800 issue binding restrictions. au800 warning area notifies pilots ofu800 potentially hazardous activity inu800 that airspace u8e28094 including military exercises andu800 weapons testing u8e28094 butu800 cannot legally prohibit civilian entry. pilots should treat active warning areas with theu800 same caution asu800 moas andu800 contact atcu800 foru800 current activity information before entering. temporary reserved area trau800 temporary reserved area trau800 temporary reserved area trau800 au800 temporary reserved area isu800 au800 defined volume ofu800 airspace that isu800  temporarily reserved foru800 theu800 exclusive oru800 priority useu800 ofu800 au800 specific aviation authority oru800 user  normally foru800 au800 limited andu800 published period ofu800 time. unlike au800 permanently restricted area au800 trau800 isu800 au800 flexible structure activated through preu800 tactical coordination u8e28094 typically theu800 dayu800 before operations u8e28094 andu800 published inu800 notams. itu800 isu800 primarily au800 european icao concept used under theu800 flexible useu800 ofu800 airspace fuau800 framework. crucially au800 trau800 isu800 notu800 necessarily impenetrable depending onu800 theu800 specific designation other traffic mayu800 beu800 permitted tou800 transit theu800 area ifu800 coordinated with theu800 airspace user oru800 theu800 relevant atcu800 authority. this distinguishes itu800 from au800 temporary segregated area tsau800 inu800 which transit byu800 nonu800 participating aircraft isu800 notu800 permitted atu800 allu800. inu800 practice tras areu800 most commonly associated with military training exercises that occur onu800 au800 recurring butu800 nonu800 permanent basis. temporary segregated area tsau800 temporary segregated area tsau800 temporary segregated area tsau800 au800 temporary segregated area isu800 theu800 more restrictive counterpart tou800 theu800 trau800. when au800 tsau800 isu800 active  nou800 nonu800 participating aircraft mayu800 transit theu800