(176,'tactical turns',' introduction tactical formation turns areu800 au800 core part ofu800 section level fighter employment. inu800 theu800 fu800 14u800 they areu800 notu800 just formation manoeuvres. they areu800 tools used tou800 preserve mutual support maintain radar andu800 visual coverage manage spacing andu800 reposition theu800 section efficiently inu800 response tou800 threats oru800 tasking. many crews know theu800 names ofu800 these turns butu800 fewer understand theu800 geometry behind them. that isu800 au800 problem because these manoeuvres only work when both aircraft understand notu800 only what turn isu800 being called butu800 also whyu800 itu800 isu800 being used andu800 howu800 theu800 geometry isu800 supposed tou800 develop. au800 section that performs theu800 wrong turn oru800 performs theu800 correct turn poorly will lose spacing lose visual support reduce sensor coverage andu800 mayu800 even create au800 midu800 airu800 risk. this page defines theu800 four most important tactical formation turns foru800 squadron useu800 theu800 check turn tacu800 turn hook turn andu800 cross turn. itu800 also explains when each should beu800 used andu800 what fu800 14u800 crews should beu800 trying tou800 achieve with them. general purpose ofu800 tactical turns general purpose ofu800 tactical turns general purpose ofu800 tactical turns tactical turns areu800 used tou800 change theu800 heading ofu800 au800 twou800 ship formation without giving upu800 tactical effectiveness. inu800 practice this means theu800 section should tryu800 tou800 maintain * mutual support between both aircraft * visual contact where possible * useful radar coverage * safe formation spacing * good geometry relative tou800 theu800 threat these turns areu800 normally flown from  combat spread  usually around  0u800u82e8u800 tou800 1u800u82e5u800 nmu800  depending onu800 theu800 tactical situation weather threat andu800 crew proficiency. theu800 correct turn depends onu800 three main factors #  howu800 large theu800 heading change isu800  #  where theu800 threat isu800 relative tou800 theu800 formation  #  what type ofu800 coverage oru800 posture theu800 section wants tou800 preserve   check turn   check turn   check turn   purpose   purpose   purpose  theu800 check turn isu800 used foru800 small heading corrections without significantly changing formation geometry.  when tou800 useu800 itu800   when tou800 useu800 itu800   when tou800 useu800 itu800  au800 check turn isu800 appropriate foru800 minor changes inu800 direction such asu800 capu800 station corrections small navigation changes oru800 slight intercept adjustments. asu800 au800 rule itu800 isu800 best used foru800 heading changes ofu800 about 30u8c2b0 oru800 less.  geometry   geometry   geometry  inu800 au800 check turn both aircraft turn inu800 theu800 same direction atu800 theu800 same time. itu800 isu800 theu800 simplest ofu800 theu800 tactical turns andu800 requires theu800 least coordination. because both aircraft turn together theu800 formation remains easy tou800 manage during small heading changes.  advantages   advantages   advantages  theu800 check turn isu800 simple quick andu800 causes minimal disruption when only au800 small correction isu800 needed.  disadvantages   disadvantages   disadvantages  ifu800 used foru800 larger heading changes spacing andu800 geometry will begin tou800 degrade. itu800 also does less tou800 preserve full threat coverage during theu800 turn than more formal tactical manoeuvres .   fu800 14u800 notes   fu800 14u800 notes   fu800 14u800 notes  foru800 tomcat crews theu800 check turn isu800 most useful foru800 routine capu800 management small awgu800 9u800 search adjustments andu800 minor repositioning when au800 full tactical turn would beu800 unnecessary. tacu800 turn tacu800 turn tacu800 turn purpose purpose purpose theu800 tacu800 turn isu800 used tou800 reposition theu800 section through  90u8c2b0  while maintaining mutual support andu800 tactical usefulness. when tou800 useu800 itu800 when tou800 useu800 itu800 when tou800 useu800 itu800 au800 tacu800 turn isu800 commonly used when theu800 threat target oru800 required newu800 heading lies roughly abeam ofu800 theu800 formation. itu800 isu800 au800 standard manoeuvre foru800 bvru800 repositioning heading changes during intercepts andu800 sector reorientation. geometry geometry geometry inu800 au800 tacu800 turn theu800  outside aircraft turns first . theu800  inside aircraft delays itsu800 turn  until theu800 outside aircraft approaches au800  nose onu800  position relative tou800 itu800. this timing isu800 what preserves tactical geometry. during theu800 manoeuvre theu800 aircraft will  swap sides . that isu800 normal andu800 should beu800 expected. advantages advantages advantages theu800 tacu800 turn allows au800 fast repositioning while preserving offensive posture andu800 mutual support. itu800 isu800 especially useful when theu800 section needs tou800 react tou800 au800 tactical picture without losing structure. disadvantages disadvantages disadvantages itu800 requires practice andu800 good timing. ifu800 airspeeds differ oru800 ifu800 oneu800 aircraft turns toou800 early oru800 toou800 late spacing canu800 degrade quickly. fu800 14u800 notes fu800 14u800 notes fu800 14u800 notes foru800 fu800 14u800 operations theu800 tacu800 turn isu800 especially useful foru800 * bvru800 commits * repositioning towards au800 braa call * sector changes during capu800 oru800 barcap * tactical heading changes during intercept timelines tomcat crews should beu800 disciplined with timing here. theu800 awgu800 9u800 gives theu800 section strong long range capability butu800 poor tacu800 turn execution will still damage formation support andu800 complicate theu800 intercept. hook turn hook turn hook turn purpose purpose purpose theu800 hook turn isu800 used foru800 large formation heading changes oru800 controlled 180u8c2b0 reversals while keeping theu800 section together. when tou800 useu800 itu800 when tou800 useu800 itu800 when tou800 useu800 itu800 useu800 au800 hook turn foru800 capu800 reversals barcap flow bvru800 repositioning oru800 anyu800 situation where theu800 section must turn together without crossing flight paths. geometry geometry geometry inu800 au800 hook turn both aircraft turn  tou800 theu800 same side atu800 theu800 same time . both aircraft select  milu800 power  andu800 flyu800 au800 tight controlled turn. theu800 aimu800 isu800 tou800 turn efficiently without gaining oru800 losing airspeed. dou800 notu800 pull sou800 hard that theu800 aircraft bleeds energy butu800 dou800 notu800 make theu800 turn sou800 wide that theu800 section becomes slow tou800 reposition. advantages advantages advantages theu800 hook turn isu800 simple predictable andu800 useful foru800 controlled reversals. disadvantages disadvantages disadvantages poor power oru800 turn management canu800 cause spacing problems. ifu800 theu800 turn isu800 toou800 soft itu800 wastes airspace. ifu800 itu800 isu800 toou800 hard theu800 aircraft loses airspeed andu800 becomes vulnerable. fu800 14u800 notes fu800 14u800 notes fu800 14u800 notes foru800 theu800 fu800 14u800 flyu800 theu800 hook turn inu800  milu800 power  with anu800 energy sustaining turn.  fu800 14u800 employment considerations   fu800 14u800 employment considerations   fu800 14u800 employment considerations  inu800 theu800 fu800 14u800 tactical turns must always beu800 considered together with radar employment timeline management andu800 crew coordination. theu800 aircraftu8e28099s long range intercept capability isu800 only useful ifu800 theu800 section keeps good tactical geometry. au800 poor turn mayu800 temporarily blind part ofu800 theu800 formation degrade mutual support oru800 force oneu800 aircraft outu800 ofu800 position during anu800 intercept. tomcat crews should therefore think about tactical turns inu800 theu800 following wayu800 * check turn foru800 small corrections with minimal disruption * tacu800 turn foru800 efficient section repositioning during bvru800 oru800 intercept work * hook turn foru800 controlled reversals while maintaining radar andu800 visual coverage rios should understand theu800 expected geometry just asu800 well asu800 pilots. even though theu800 pilot flies theu800 turn theu800 riou800 should help maintain tactical awareness call spacing concerns andu800 support theu800 leadu8e28099s plan. '),
(177,'vsfs 41st airu800 tou800 airu800 refueling',' purpose purpose purpose airu800 tou800 airu800 refuelling extends mission endurance increases time onu800 station andu800 allows theu800 fu800 14u800 tou800 continue operations beyond internal fuel limits. good refuelling isu800 notu800 aggressive. itu800 isu800 stable formation flying with careful closure control. preu800 contact setup preu800 contact setup preu800 contact setup before joining theu800 tanker configure theu800 aircraft * wing sweep  auto official bomb   * autopilot  offu800  * probe  outu800  * exterior lights  asu800 briefed  * tanker frequency tacan  confirmed  theu800 aircraft must beu800  nose cold  around theu800 tanker * master armu800  safe  * acmu800 cover  closed  * nou800 airu800 tou800 airu800 lock * nou800 airu800 tou800 ground delivery mode join upu800 join upu800 join upu800 join from  below andu800 behind  theu800 tanker. dou800 notu800 approach from above. move tou800 theu800 observation position normally onu800 theu800  left side ofu800 theu800 tanker  slightly aftu800 andu800 stable. foru800 kcu800 130u800 operations stay clear ofu800 prop wash until cleared inu800. closure control closure control closure control most failed tankings start with toou800 much closure. useu800 theu800 rule  closure rate u8e28988 distance u8c397 100u800  examples * 1u800u82e0u800 nmu800 u8e28692 100u800 knots closure * 0u800u82e5u800 nmu800 u8e28692 50u800 knots closure * 0u800u82e2u800 nmu800 u8e28692 20u800 knots closure * 0u800u82e1u800 nmu800 u8e28692 10u800 knots closure theu800 closer youu800 areu800 theu800 slower youu800 close. inside theu800 basket area closure should beu800 only  2u8e280935 knots . contact technique contact technique contact technique when cleared preu800 contact move forward slowly andu800 stabilise. useu800 theu800 controls correctly *  throttle controls closure  *  stick controls position  *  trim reduces workload  flyu800 theu800 aircraft into theu800 basket. dou800 notu800 chase theu800 basket. theu800 drogue moves; theu800 tanker isu800 theu800 stable reference. theu800 riou800 usualy helps with alignement with theu800 basket. look atu800 theu800  tanker basket andu800 reference points . dou800 notu800 stare atu800 theu800 probe. staring atu800 theu800 probe usually causes overcontrolling. dou800 notu800 stab theu800 basket. useu800 small corrections andu800 gentle forward movement. inu800 contact inu800 contact inu800 contact once connected stop trying tou800 u8e2809cpushu8e2809d into theu800 basket. flyu800 formation onu800 theu800 tanker. make only small corrections * small power change * wait * observe * correct again ifu800 needed theu800 fu800 14u800 isu800 heavy andu800 slow tou800 respond. large throttle oru800 stick inputs usually create oscillations andu800 disconnects. disconnect disconnect disconnect foru800 au800 normal disconnect reduce power slightly letu800 theu800 basket separate naturally then move down andu800 away from theu800 tanker onto theu800 waiting area. ifu800 unstable ordered tou800 disconnect oru800 losing situational awareness # disconnect # move down # move away from theu800 tanker # regain stable flight # rejoin safely dou800 notu800 pull aggressively away unless required foru800 safety. fu800 14u800 specific notes fu800 14u800 specific notes fu800 14u800 specific notes theu800 tomcat hasu800 significant inertia especially when heavy with fuel. think ahead ofu800 theu800 aircraft andu800 avoid late corrections. sou800  useu800 that trim   theu800 probe isu800 faru800 forward ofu800 theu800 pilotu8e28099s seating position. donu800\'tu800 overcorrect lateral alignment. small inputs areu800 usually enough. donu800\'tu800 input more than oneu800 dimension ofu800 movement. fixu800 oneu800 dimension atu800 au800 time. rules ofu800 thumb rules ofu800 thumb rules ofu800 thumb * nose cold * probe outu800 * join from below andu800 behind * closure distance u8c397 100u800 * throttle controls closure * stick controls position * trim isu800 your friend * flyu800 theu800 tanker notu800 theu800 basket * small corrections only ');
