(204,'== 01 / Installing SRS ==\n\n=== 01. DOWNLOAD srs iNSTALLER ===\n You can download SRS from [https://github.com/ciribob/DCS-SimpleRadioStandalone/releases here] | Make sure the version has Latest in Green to the right of it.\n\n=== 02. INSTALL SRS ===\n Installation is pretty straightforward. Unzip SRS and run Installer.exe. SRS should automatically point to the Saved Games folder if not point to your DCS Saved Games folder\n  (C:\\Users\\{your-username-here]\\Saved Games) <- Should look something like this. If you look for it manually the folders are visually named by your local windows language so make sure to translate accordingly! After that you can click \"Install/Update DCS-SRS\" button!\n\n== 02 / srs settings ==\n\n=== 01. radio keybinds ===\n Click on Controls\n[[File:SRS General Edited.png|left|frameless|465x465px]]\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n Then bind Radio 1 & 2 and 3 & 4 if your an F/A-18C Pilot (You can bind the radio keybind to your HOTAS like you see on the screen but as far as i know only to one device)\n[[File:SRS Controls.png|left|thumb|466x466px]]','utf-8'),
