(525,'== History ==\nThe S-125 Newa (russian С-125 \'\'Нева\'\', NATO-Codename: \'\'\'SA-3 GOA) is a radar guided surface to air rocket system with a two staged rocket, produced in the Sowjet Union. It was developed by the Isajew construction office and came into service in 1961 among the forces of the Warschauer Pakt\'\'\'\n\nIt was supposed be more agile and so on more effective against fast moving targets than the SA-2 \n\n== Units ==\n\n=== Passive Units ===\n\n=== Truck GAZ-66 ===\nIs a simple military all terrain vehicle to supply the SAM site with everything needed\n[[File:ParkPatriot2015part4-22.jpg|center|thumb|666x666px]]\n\n=== GPU on Ural Truck ===\nThe GPU is supplying the SAM site with electric power\n[[File:Apa-1.jpg|center|thumb|697x697px]]\nMobile Command Center on Truck\n\nThe command center operates the SAM site and recieves the orders. The launches are organized from there. It also contains the radar operators.\n[[File:Zil131 nva.jpg|center|thumb|696x696px]]\n\n=== Active Units ===\n\n=== Launcher ===\nThe lauchers host and launch the rockets. The easiest way to identify a SAM visually is by knowing what the launcher with the rocket looks like. The SA-3 Launcher Hosts 4 Rockets.\n[[File:5P73-Launcher-Deployed-MiroslavGyurosi-1S.jpg|center|thumb|698x698px]]\n{| class=\"wikitable\"\n|+Tactical Data\n!Size\n!Speed\n!Min Range\n!MAx Range\n!Min Alt\n!Max Alt\n!Seeker Head\n|-\n|6.1 Meters\n|Mach 3.5\n|TBC\n|11.2 Miles\n|700 feet\n|20500 feet\n|None\n|}\n\n=== SA-3 Search radar \"Flat Face ===\nThe Flat Face search radar scans the airspace around the SAM site fpr enemy fighters and transmitts the contacts over to the track radar. Is able to provide bearing and range of airborne contacts up to 85 Nautical Miles.\n[[File:TechMuseumToliatti-1813-X2.jpg|center|thumb|692x692px]]\n\n=== SA-3 TRack Radar \"Low Blow\" ===\nhe Trackradar guides launches and the rockets after the launch. It only turns during the lock establishment and according to the fighters movements. Track range goes up to 22 Nautical Miles.\n[[File:Ad sam s125 p01.jpg|center|thumb|400x400px]]','utf-8'),
(526,'== Available tankers (Source Training Theatre) ==\n[[File:US Navy 030125-N-0905V-002 S-3B \'Viking assigned to the Screwbirds of Sea Control Squadron 33 (VS-33) .jpg|left|thumb|272x272px|Lockheed S-3B Viking]]','utf-8'),
(527,'__NOTOC__\n__NOEDITSECTION__\n\n<!-- HERO -->\n<div style=\"border:1px solid #c8c5bf; padding:48px 32px 36px 32px; margin-bottom:32px; text-align:center;\">\n<div style=\"font-size:0.6rem; letter-spacing:5px; color:#9a9690; margin-bottom:20px;\">&#9632;&#9632;&#9632; UNCLASSIFIED — FOR SOURCE MEMBERS ONLY &#9632;&#9632;&#9632;</div>\n<div style=\"border-top:1px solid #c8c5bf; max-width:200px; margin:0 auto 24px auto;\"></div>\n[[File:Sourcelogosmall.png|100px|center|link=]]\n<div style=\"font-size:1.6rem; font-weight:600; letter-spacing:8px; margin:20px 0 8px 0;\">SOURCE DCS</div>\n<div style=\"font-size:0.72rem; letter-spacing:4px; color:#4a4845; margin-bottom:20px;\">SHADOW OPERATIONS - UNDERSTANDING REAL COMBAT ENVIRONMENTS</div>\n<div style=\"border-top:1px solid #c8c5bf; max-width:200px; margin:0 auto 16px auto;\"></div>\n<div style=\"font-size:0.62rem; letter-spacing:2px; color:#9a9690;\">\nCURRENT THEATER: SYRIA - \n[[Server Info/Airfields|AIRFIELDS]] - [[Theater/DTC-INFO|DTCINFO]]\n</div>\n</div>\n\n----\n\n== 01 / Personnel Onboarding ==\n\nNew to SOURCE? Complete all onboarding steps before your first operation. Install required software, read the rules of engagement, and familiarize yourself with communications procedures.\n\n[[Guides/New Member Guide|New Member Guide]] · [[Guides/SRS Setup|SRS Setup]] · [[Guides/Mod Installation|Mod Installation]]\n\n== 02 / General Knowledge ==\nContains all the Knowledge about the threats we could Face along with tactics to evade an neutralize.\n\n[[SAM Surface to Air Missile]] · [[How To Read Charts]] · [[GENERAL/Airspace Classifications|Airspace Classes]] \n\n----\n\n== 03 / multi-Service tactics, techniques, and procedures (MTTP) ==\n\nAll personnel are expected to operate within SOURCE standard procedures.\n\n=== Communication ===\n\'\'\'IN CASE OF DOUBT USE PLAIN LANGUAGE\'\'\'\n\n[[General/Tactical Communication Revision 1|Tactical Communication]] · [[General/Air Traffic Communication|Air Traffic Communication]] · [[DDFORM1801|Filing Flight Plans]]  · [[MTTP/ACC/Training Range Communications|Training Range Communication]] \n\n=== CLOSE AIR SUPPORT ===\nTO BE ADDED\n\nFor Unit-Specific Procedures reference SQUADRON STANDARD OPERATING PROCEDURES below\n\n----\n\n== 04 / Squadron STANDARD OPERATING PROCEDURES ==\n\n{| class=\"wikitable\" style=\"width:100%;\"\n|-\n! Squadron !! Aircraft\n|-\n| [[Squadrons/78th VMRS Shadow Knights|78th VMRS Shadow Knights]] || F-16C Viper\n|-\n| [[14th VSFS Top Hatters]]|| F/A-18C Hornet\n|-\n| [[Squadrons/509th VSFS Black Anvils|509th VSFS Black Anvils]] || F-15E Strike Eagle\n|}\n\n----\n\n== 05 / Active Operations ==\n\nCurrent campaign briefings, mission assignments, and sortie records are maintained in the operations section. All flight leads are responsible for keeping mission pages up to date following each operation.\n\n[[Campaigns|View All Campaigns]]','utf-8'),
