(538,'== What is cAS? ==\n[[File:An-fa-18-hornet-aircraft-assigned-to-the-strike-aircraft-test-directorate-of-058115-1024.jpg|thumb|298x298px]]\nClose Air Support (CAS) is when fixed or rotary-wing aircraft attack hostile targets that are in close proximity to friendly forces, with each mission requiring detailed coordination with the fire and movement of those forces on the ground. \n\nIt\'s not just about dropping bombs near the front line, every turn, every trigger squeeze, every weapon employed is deliberate. Every attack has to be carefully coordinated so that airpower and ground forces are working as one, which is what separates CAS from other air-to-ground missions like interdiction. It\'s considered one of the most demanding missions in military aviation precisely because the margin for error is essentially zero.','utf-8'),
(539,'12stepCAS','utf-8'),
(540,'== What is CAS? ==\n[[File:An-fa-18-hornet-aircraft-assigned-to-the-strike-aircraft-test-directorate-of-058115-1024.jpg|thumb|298x298px|left]]\nClose Air Support (CAS) is when fixed or rotary-wing aircraft attack hostile targets that are in close proximity to friendly forces, with each mission requiring detailed coordination with the fire and movement of those forces on the ground. It\'s not just about dropping bombs near the front line, every turn, every trigger squeeze, every weapon employed is deliberate.  \n\nThe person who makes that happen is the JTAC — Joint Terminal Attack Controller — a specially trained operator embedded with ground forces who spots the target, radios the pilot with everything they need to know, and gives the final word to fire. No clearance from the JTAC, no bombs drop — period. Every attack has to be carefully coordinated so that airpower and ground forces are working as one, which is what separates CAS from other air-to-ground missions like interdiction. It\'s considered one of the most demanding missions in military aviation precisely because the margin for error is essentially zero.  \n\n== Order of eventS ==\n<big>The \'\'\'\"12-step CAS Procedure\"\'\'\' is a simplified way to breakdown the order of events that occur in a standard CAS mission.</big> \n[[File:Image 2026-06-27 172410529.png|thumb]]\n\n# \'\'\'<big>Routing/Safety of Flight</big>\'\'\'\n# \'\'\'<big>Aircraft Check-in</big>\'\'\'\n# \'\'\'<big>Situation Update (SITUP)</big>\'\'\'\n# \'\'\'<big>Game Plan</big>\'\'\'\n# \'\'\'<big>9-line</big>\'\'\'\n# \'\'\'<big>Remarks/Restrictions</big>\'\'\'\n# \'\'\'<big>Readbacks</big>\'\'\'\n# \'\'\'<big>Correlation</big>\'\'\'\n# \'\'\'<big>Attack Phase</big>\'\'\'\n# \'\'\'<big>Asses Effects (BDA specific to the previous engagement)</big>\'\'\'\n# \'\'\'<big>Final BDA (Mission summary BDA)</big>\'\'\'\n# \'\'\'<big>Routing/Safety of Flight</big>\'\'\'','utf-8'),
(541,'== What is CAS? ==\n[[File:An-fa-18-hornet-aircraft-assigned-to-the-strike-aircraft-test-directorate-of-058115-1024.jpg|thumb|298x298px|left]]\nClose Air Support (CAS) is when fixed or rotary-wing aircraft attack hostile targets that pose a threat and is in close proximity to nearby friendlies, with each mission requiring detailed coordination with the fire and movement of those forces on the ground. It\'s not just about dropping bombs near the front line. Every turn, every trigger squeeze, every weapon employed is deliberate.  \n\nThe person who makes that happen is the JTAC (Joint Terminal Attack Controller), a specially trained operator who spots the target, radios the pilot with everything they need to know, and gives the final word to fire. While a JTAC is typically on the ground, a qualified JTAC pilot can also control from the air in a role known as FAC(A), or Forward Air Controller (Airborne).   \n\nEvery attack has to be carefully coordinated so that airpower and ground forces are working as one, which is what separates CAS from other air-to-ground missions like Air Interdiction. It\'s considered one of the most demanding missions in military aviation precisely because the margin for error is essentially zero.  \n\n== Order of Events (12-Step CAS Procedure) ==\n<big>The \'\'\'\"12-step CAS Procedure\"\'\'\' is a simplified way to breakdown the general order of events that occur in a standard CAS mission.</big> \n[[File:Image 2026-06-27 172410529.png|thumb]]\n\n# \'\'\'<big>Routing/Safety of Flight</big>\'\'\'\n# \'\'\'<big>Aircraft Check-in</big>\'\'\'\n# \'\'\'<big>Situation Update (SITUP)</big>\'\'\'\n# \'\'\'<big>Game Plan</big>\'\'\'\n# \'\'\'<big>9-line</big>\'\'\'\n# \'\'\'<big>Remarks/Restrictions</big>\'\'\'\n# \'\'\'<big>Readbacks</big>\'\'\'\n# \'\'\'<big>Correlation</big>\'\'\'\n# \'\'\'<big>Attack Phase</big>\'\'\'\n# \'\'\'<big>Asses Effects (BDA specific to the previous engagement)</big>\'\'\'\n# \'\'\'<big>Final BDA (Mission summary BDA)</big>\'\'\'\n# \'\'\'<big>Routing/Safety of Flight</big>\'\'\'','utf-8'),
(542,'{{DISPLAYTITLE:Squadrons/14th VSFS Top Hatters}}\n{{DISPLAYTITLE:14th VSFS Top Hatters}}\n{{DISPLAYTITLE:14th VSFS Top Hatters}}\n\n= 14TH VSFS special operating procedures =\n\n== Overview ==\n[[File:Screen 260330 155302 4.png|thumb|387x387px]]\nThe 14th Virtual Strike Fighter Squadron (VSFS) \"Top Hatters\" is a carrier-based F/A-18C strike fighter squadron deployed aboard the USS Harry S. Truman (CVN-75). The squadron takes its name, identity, and doctrine, from VFA-14 \"Top Hatters\": the US Navy\'s oldest continuously active squadron, founded in 1919 and known as \"The Oldest and the Boldest.\" \n\n14th VSFS strives to honour that century-long legacy by upholding the professionalism, discipline, and tactical excellence of the real Top Hatters, with authentic US Navy carrier procedures adapted into all virtual operations.\n\n== Carrier Operations and Procedures ==\n[[File:Screen 260405 152707.png|left|thumb|429x429px]]\nThe USS Harry S. Truman is the beating heart of our operations. All mission-ready pilots in our squadron are expected to be comfortable operating to, on, and from the carrier. Below you will find useful guides and resources to conduct safe and efficient carrier operations. \n\n[[14th VSFS/Case I Procedures|Case I Procedures (work in progress)]]\n\n[[14th VSFS/Case III Procedures|Case III Procedures (work in progress)]]\n\n[[General/CATC Communications Guide|Carrier Communications and Phraseology (CATCC)]]\n\n[[Landing Signal Officer (LSO) Guide]]\n\n== Tactical Procedures (WIP) ==\n[[File:Screen 260330 155406.png|thumb|510x510px]]\n\'\'\'<u>Tactical Procedures will cover how we fight together.</u>\'\'\'\n\nAir to Ground Tactics\n\n* [[14th VSFS/Close Air Support (CAS)|Close Air Support (CAS)]]\n* [[Strike/Air Interdiction]]\n* [[SEAD/DEAD]]\n* [[Anti-Ship]]<br />\n\nAir to Air Tactics\n\n* [[Tactical Turns]]\n* [[Beyond Visual Range (BVR)]]\n* [[Basic Fighter Maneuvers (BFM)]]\n* [[Combat Air Patrol (CAP)]]<br />\n\n== General Flight Procedures (WIP) ==\n[[File:Screen 260327 220735.png|thumb|464x464px|left]]\n\'\'\'<u>General Flight Procedures will cover how we fly together.</u>\'\'\'\n\n[[Airfield operations (Shore-based)]]\n\n[[Formation Flying]]\n\n[[14th VSFS/Air to Air Refueling|Air to Air Refueling]]\n\n[[Advanced Fuel Management]]\n\n[[Night Flying]]\n\n\n\n\n\n== Resources and Files ==\nTIP: CTRL+CLICK on any link to open it in a new tab instead of replacing this one\n\n[https://polybox.ethz.ch/index.php/s/S8Es6KCzBao5WYm/download?path=%2FLiveries&files=14th%20VSFS%20Top%20Hatters%20HiVis%20V1.0-20260330T154252Z-3-001.zip 14th VSFS Standard Livery]\n\n[https://polybox.ethz.ch/index.php/s/S8Es6KCzBao5WYm/download?path=%2FKneeboards&files=FA-18C_hornet.rar 14th VSFS Kneeboard (Checklists + Quick Reference Guides + LTAG Aerodrome and Tacan Approach Charts)]\n\n[https://chucksguides.com/aircraft/dcs/fa-18c/ Chucks Guides - F/A-18C Hornet]\n\n[https://info.publicintelligence.net/F18-ABCD-000.pdf NATOPS FLIGHT MANUAL F/A-18A/B/C/D A1-F18AC-NFM-000] (Sept, 2008)\n\n[https://www.digitalcombatsimulator.com/upload/iblock/ea9/lxf69u2uk1fhqq7ndb55z9egzabe8hdg/DCS%20FA-18C%20Early%20Access%20Guide%20EN.pdf Eagle Dynamics F/A-18C Early Access Guide] (March, 2024)\n\n{{DEFAULTSORT:Squadrons/14th VSFS Top Hatters}}','utf-8'),
(543,'__NOTOC__\n__NOEDITSECTION__\n\n<!-- HERO -->\n<div style=\"border:1px solid #c8c5bf; padding:48px 32px 36px 32px; margin-bottom:32px; text-align:center;\">\n<div style=\"font-size:0.6rem; letter-spacing:5px; color:#9a9690; margin-bottom:20px;\">&#9632;&#9632;&#9632; UNCLASSIFIED — FOR SOURCE MEMBERS ONLY &#9632;&#9632;&#9632;</div>\n<div style=\"border-top:1px solid #c8c5bf; max-width:200px; margin:0 auto 24px auto;\"></div>\n[[File:Sourcelogosmall.png|100px|center|link=]]\n<div style=\"font-size:1.6rem; font-weight:600; letter-spacing:8px; margin:20px 0 8px 0;\">SOURCE DCS</div>\n<div style=\"font-size:0.72rem; letter-spacing:4px; color:#4a4845; margin-bottom:20px;\">SHADOW OPERATIONS - UNDERSTANDING REAL COMBAT ENVIRONMENTS</div>\n<div style=\"border-top:1px solid #c8c5bf; max-width:200px; margin:0 auto 16px auto;\"></div>\n<div style=\"font-size:0.62rem; letter-spacing:2px; color:#9a9690;\">\nCURRENT THEATER: SYRIA - \n[[Server Info/Airfields|AIRFIELDS]] - [[Theater/DTC-INFO|DTCINFO]]\n</div>\n</div>\n\n----\n\n== 01 / Personnel Onboarding ==\n\nNew to SOURCE? Complete all onboarding steps before your first operation. Install required software, read the rules of engagement, and familiarize yourself with communications procedures.\n\n[[Guides/New Member Guide|New Member Guide]] · [[Guides/SRS Setup|SRS Setup]] · [[Guides/Mod Installation|Mod Installation]]\n\n== 02 / General Knowledge ==\nContains all the Knowledge about the threats we could Face along with tactics to evade an neutralize.\n\n[[SAM Surface to Air Missile]] · [[How To Read Charts]] · [[GENERAL/Airspace Classifications|Airspace Classes]] \n\n----\n\n== 03 / multi-Service tactics, techniques, and procedures (MTTP) ==\n\nAll personnel are expected to operate within SOURCE standard procedures.\n\n=== Communication ===\n\'\'\'IN CASE OF DOUBT USE PLAIN LANGUAGE\'\'\'\n\n[[General/Tactical Communication Revision 1|Tactical Communication]] · [[General/Air Traffic Communication|Air Traffic Communication]] · [[DDFORM1801|Filing Flight Plans]]  · [[MTTP/ACC/Training Range Communications|Training Range Communication]] \n\n=== CLOSE AIR SUPPORT ===\nTO BE ADDED\n\nFor Unit-Specific Procedures reference SQUADRON STANDARD OPERATING PROCEDURES below\n\n----\n\n== 04 / Squadron STANDARD OPERATING PROCEDURES ==\n\n{| class=\"wikitable\" style=\"width:100%;\"\n|-\n! Squadron !! Aircraft\n|-\n| [[Squadrons/78th VMRS Shadow Knights|78th VMRS Shadow Knights]] || F-16C Viper\n|-\n| [[14th VSFS Top Hatters]]|| F/A-18C Hornet\n|-\n| [[Squadrons/509th VSFS Black Anvils|509th VSFS Black Anvils]] || F-15E Strike Eagle\n|-\n|[[41st VSFS Black Aces]]\n|F-14B(U) Tomcat\n|}\n\n----\n\n== 05 / Active Operations ==\n\nCurrent campaign briefings, mission assignments, and sortie records are maintained in the operations section. All flight leads are responsible for keeping mission pages up to date following each operation.\n\n[[Campaigns|View All Campaigns]]','utf-8'),
(544,'{{DISPLAYTITLE:Squadrons/41st Black Aces}} {{DISPLAYTITLE:41st VSFS Black Aces}} {{DISPLAYTITLE:41st VSFS Black Aces}}\n\n= 41st VSFS special operating procedures =\n\n== Overview ==\n[[File:Screen_260330_155302_4.png|thumb|387x387px]]\nThe 41st Virtual Strike Fighter Squadron (VSFS) \"Black Aces\" is a carrier-based F-14B(U) strike fighter squadron deployed aboard the USS Harry S. Truman (CVN-75). <u>The squadron takes its name, identity, and doctrine, from VFA-14 \"Top Hatters\": the US Navy\'s oldest continuously active squadron, founded in 1919 and known as \"The Oldest and the Boldest.\"</u>\n\n<u>14th VSFS strives to honour that century-long legacy by upholding the professionalism, discipline, and tactical excellence of the real Top Hatters, with authentic US Navy carrier procedures adapted into all virtual operations.</u>\n\n== Carrier Operations and Procedures ==\n[[File:Screen_260405_152707.png|left|thumb|429x429px]]\nThe USS Harry S. Truman is the beating heart of our operations. All mission-ready pilots in our squadron are expected to be comfortable operating to, on, and from the carrier. Below you will find useful guides and resources to conduct safe and efficient carrier operations.\n\n[[41st VSFS/Case I Procedures|Case I Procedures (work in progress)]]\n\n[[41st VSFS/Case III Procedures|Case III Procedures (work in progress)]]\n\n[[General/CATC Communications Guide|Carrier Communications and Phraseology (CATCC)]]\n\n[[Landing Signal Officer (LSO) Guide]]\n\n== Tactical Procedures (WIP) ==\n[[File:Screen_260330_155406.png|thumb|510x510px]]\n\'\'\'<u>Tactical Procedures will cover how we fight together.</u>\'\'\'\n\nAir to Ground Tactics\n\n* [[14th VSFS/Close Air Support (CAS)|Close Air Support (CAS)]]\n* [[Strike/Air Interdiction]]\n* [[SEAD/DEAD]]\n* [[Anti-Ship]]\n\nAir to Air Tactics\n\n* [[Tactical Turns]]\n* [[Beyond Visual Range (BVR)]]\n* [[Basic Fighter Maneuvers (BFM)]]\n* [[Combat Air Patrol (CAP)]]\n\n== General Flight Procedures (WIP) ==\n[[File:Screen_260327_220735.png|left|thumb|464x464px]]\n\'\'\'<u>General Flight Procedures will cover how we fly together.</u>\'\'\'\n\n[[Airfield operations (Shore-based)]]\n\n[[Formation Flying]]\n\n[[14th VSFS/Air to Air Refueling|Air to Air Refueling]]\n\n[[Advanced Fuel Management]]\n\n[[Night Flying]]\n\n== Resources and Files ==\nTIP: CTRL+CLICK on any link to open it in a new tab instead of replacing this one\n\n[Link to livery, when livery]\n\n[https://polybox.ethz.ch/index.php/s/S8Es6KCzBao5WYm/download?path=%2FKneeboards&files=FA-18C_hornet.rar <u>14th VSFS Kneeboard (Checklists + Quick Reference Guides + LTAG Aerodrome and Tacan Approach Charts)</u>]\n\n[https://chucksguides.com/aircraft/dcs/f-14b/#&#x5B;1,%22XYZ%22,0,540,1&#x5D; Chucks Guides - F-14B] \n\n[https://server.3rd-wing.net/public/Bureau_VF31/Docs%20F-14%20r%C3%A9el/NAVAIR%2001-F14AAP-1%20-%20NATOPS%20Flight%20Manual%20-%20F-14B.pdf NATOPS FLIGHT MANUAL 01-F14AAP-1] (Aug, 2001)\n\n[https://f14.manuals.heatblur.se/ Heatblur F-14 Manual] (June, 2026)','utf-8'),
(545,'== Source Training Theatre ==\n\n=== FREQUENCies ===\n{| class=\"wikitable\"\n|+F-16C Shadow Knights\n!<big>Station\\setting</big>\n!<big>FREQUENCY</big>\n!<big>CHAN</big>\n|-\n|<big>Common</big>\n|<big>251.000</big>\n|<big>1</big>\n|-\n|<big>LTAG TWR</big>\n|<big>360.200</big>\n|<big>2</big>\n|-\n|<big>LTAG RADAR</big>\n|<big>340.775</big>\n|<big>3</big>\n|-\n|<big>LTAG PRECISION</big>\n|<big>282.500</big>\n|<big>4</big>\n|-\n|<big>LTAG ATIS</big>\n|<big>377.475</big>\n|<big>5</big>\n|-\n|<big>MAGIC</big>\n|<big>261.500</big>\n|<big>6</big>\n|-\n|<big>CV-75 MRSHL</big>\n|<big>307.500</big>\n|<big>7</big>\n|-\n|<big>Carrier Frequencys</big>\n|\n|<big>8-10</big>\n|-\n|<big>Tankers</big>\n|\n|<big>11-14</big>\n|-\n|<big>Unit Option</big>\n|\n|<big>15-20</big>\n|}\n{| class=\"wikitable\"\n|+F/A-18C Top Hatters\n!\n!<big>Frequency</big>\n!<big>CHAN</big>\n|-\n|<big>CVN-75 Pri-Fly (TWR)</big>\n|<big>307.500</big>\n|<big>1</big>\n|-\n|<big>CVN-75 Departure</big>\n|<big>315.500</big>\n|<big>2</big>\n|-\n|<big>Magic</big>\n|<big>261.500</big>\n|<big>3</big>\n|-\n|<big>LTAG ATIS</big>\n|<big>377.475</big>\n|<big>4</big>\n|-\n|<big>LTAG TWR</big>\n|<big>360.200</big>\n|<big>5</big>\n|-\n|<big>LTAG Radar</big>\n|<big>340.775</big>\n|<big>6</big>\n|-\n|<big>LTAG Precision</big>\n|<big>282.500</big>\n|<big>7</big>\n|-\n|<big>Common Advisory</big>\n|<big>251.000</big>\n|<big>8</big>\n|-\n|<big>LTR 1 RNG CNTL</big>\n|<big>231.540</big>\n|<big>9</big>\n|-\n|<big>LTR 2 RNG CNTL</big>\n|<big>342.775</big>\n|<big>10</big>\n|-\n|<big>LTR 3 RNG CNTL</big>\n|<big>276.5</big>\n|<big>11</big>\n|-\n|<big>LTR 4 RNG CNTL</big>\n|<big>247.8</big>\n|<big>12</big>\n|-\n|<big>LCR 6 RNG CNTL</big>\n|<big>280.175</big>\n|<big>13</big>\n|-\n|<big>AS RQRD</big>\n|<big>N/A</big>\n|<big>14</big>\n|-\n|<big>CVN-75 APP #1</big>\n|<big>339.500</big>\n|<big>15</big>\n|-\n|<big>CVN-75 Marshal</big>\n|<big>377.200</big>\n|<big>16</big>\n|-\n|<big>CVN-75 APP #2</big>\n|<big>339.600</big>\n|<big>17</big>\n|-\n|<big>SHELL 2-1</big>\n|<big>254.000</big>\n|<big>18</big>\n|-\n|<big>Mauler 6-1</big>\n|<big>311.500</big>\n|<big>19</big>\n|-\n|<big>AS RQRD</big>\n|<big>N/A</big>\n|<big>20</big>\n|}\n-----\n=== WAYPOINTS ===','utf-8'),
