, min Go 150, Go 160 (are V speeds currently not used in SK), rotation speed 200, AB off at 300, contract speed 350, 5 nose up, in case of lost Wingmen turn right for 30 seconds unsing 30 AOB, inform Lead, transition to instruments, obtain seperate ATC clearence and attempt re-join, say when airborne, you´re cleared to join on the right, say when in position.\n\n== Runway Lineup ==\nGeneral:\n\n• Leader will direct the appropriate runway line up based on winds and runway width\n\n• Wingmen should line up ensuring wingtip clearance\n\nLineup Types:\n\n• Two Ship Lineup\n\n• Three Ship Echelon\n\n• Four Ship Echelon\n\n• Four Ship three in The Slot\n\n• Four Ship four in The Slot\n\n• Three Ship three in The Slot\n\nLineup Standards:\n\n• Runway lineup is determined by taking into account several factors:\n\no Wind direction and speed\n\no Direction of turn out of traffic\n\no Weather\n\n• Minimum wingtip spacing is wingtip clearance but may be wider as desired or required\n\n== Two Ship Lineup ==\n• Lead takes the center of it´s half of the runway\n\n• The wingmen will line up lead´s main gear doors and take wingtip spacing as briefed\n[[File:STANAG7001FormationFlying.pdf – Mozilla Firefox 05.10.2025 19 39 19.png|left|692x692px|Example Two Ship Lineup|frameless]]','utf-8'),
